## Example: Anti-Pattern Node

```agm
agm: 1.0
package: api.patterns
version: 0.1.0

node api.anti_pattern.expose_internal_ids
type: anti_pattern
summary: do not expose internal sequential database IDs in public API responses
priority: high
stability: high
detail:
  Sequential integer IDs leak row counts, allow enumeration attacks, and
  create tight coupling between the API contract and the internal data model.
  Use UUIDs or opaque tokens in public-facing responses.
resolution: Replace integer primary keys in API responses with UUID surrogate keys.
see_also: [api.rules.response_contracts]
```

---

## Example: Ticket Node

```agm
agm: 1.0
package: backend.tasks
version: 0.1.0

node backend.ticket.add_rate_limit
type: ticket
summary: add per-user rate limiting to the public API endpoints
priority: high
stability: high
depends: [backend.facts.api_endpoints, backend.rules.auth]
detail:
  Implement token-bucket rate limiting at the API gateway layer.
  Limit: 100 requests per minute per authenticated user.
  Unauthenticated requests share a global bucket of 20 req/min.
  Emit a 429 response with Retry-After header when the bucket is empty.
```
